// Adversarial stress: EchoStrike protocol with Prism multi-bolt under chaos — Scatter layout.
//
// EchoStrike builds an EchoNetwork: Perfect Bumps strengthen it and cell hits
// damage it. Prism spawns multiple bolts, meaning EchoNetwork receives concurrent
// cell-hit signals from independent bolt entities. This stress scenario targets:
//
//   1. Concurrent EchoNetwork write hazard: multiple Prism bolts can hit
//      different cells within the same FixedUpdate frame, each independently
//      decrementing EchoNetwork integrity. If the system processes both writes
//      non-atomically (e.g., reading integrity, computing decrement, writing back),
//      one decrement overwrites the other. The network can never go negative, so
//      if it underflows to a wrapping value, NoNaN catches NaN propagation and
//      BoltSpeedAccurate catches any reactive speed change from a corrupted network.
//
//   2. cleanup_destroyed_echoes cross-reference integrity: when a cell is destroyed
//      that the EchoNetwork holds a component reference to, cleanup_destroyed_echoes
//      must remove all references to that entity. Under Scatter layout, cells are
//      destroyed in non-contiguous bursts — the multi-bolt Prism configuration
//      can destroy two cells simultaneously, both referenced by the EchoNetwork.
//      If only one is cleaned up, the stale reference causes a panic or NaN on next
//      network read. NoEntityLeaks catches EchoNetwork components whose backing
//      cell entities have been despawned.
//
//   3. Perfect Bump timing under chaos: action_prob 0.7 with Prism means some bolts
//      produce PerfectBumped events and some don't — the EchoNetwork strength
//      counter must only increment for confirmed Perfect Bumps, not all bumps.
//      If the PerfectBumped filter is too broad and fires on any bump, network
//      strength accumulates unboundedly, causing BoltSpeedAccurate violations
//      when strength-derived speed modifiers overflow.
//
//   4. Bolt count management: Prism produces 2+ bolts by design; Scatter layout
//      and chaos input keep both active. BoltCountReasonable (default cap 8) is
//      sufficient for Prism's standard bolt count. NoEntityLeaks guards the echo
//      component cleanup path when bolts are lost.
//
// 3000 frames with allow_early_end: false cycles through multiple Scatter layouts.
// 16 runs explore diverse multi-bolt impact orderings and cell destruction patterns.
(
    breaker: "Prism",
    layout: "Scatter",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.7)),
    max_frames: 3000,
    disallowed_failures: [
        NoNaN,
        BoltInBounds,
        BreakerInBounds,
        BoltSpeedAccurate,
        ValidDashState,
        BreakerCountReasonable,
        NoEntityLeaks,
        BoltCountReasonable,
    ],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    stress: (runs: 16, parallelism: 16),
    seed: 5527,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectProtocol(kind_name: "EchoStrike")),
    ],
)
